    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d382">

                <pb facs="0561" n="461" sameAs="frus:frus1934v01/pg461"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A14/670C: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chairman of the American
                        Delegation</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-06-20T19:00:00-04:00">June 20, 1934—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>162. Our 429, June 7, 7 p.m.<anchor n="21" xml:id="d382-f1"/> The Senate on June
                    15 gave its advice and consent to ratification but added the following
                    reservation: <pb facs="0562" n="462" xml:id="pg462"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“… subject to the reservation that the said convention shall not come
                            into force so far as the United States is concerned until it shall have
                            come into force in respect to Belgium, the British Empire,
                            Czechoslovakia, France, Germany, Italy, Japan, Sweden, and the Union of
                            Soviet Socialistic Republics, and with the further understanding that
                            such adherence to this treaty shall not be construed as denying any
                            right of sovereignty which the Kingdom of Persia may have in and to the
                            Persian Gulf or to the waters thereof.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>The portion of this reservation which pertains to the Persian Gulf was
                    unsuccessfully opposed by the Department.</p>
                <p>The Department will telegraph when the President ratifies.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
